## `bitcoin/bips` — BIP340's own test vectors

  https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0340/test-vectors.csv
  Author: Pieter Wuille <pieter.wuille@gmail.com>
  Licensed under the 2-clause BSD license (`License: BSD-2-Clause` in the BIP's
  own header).

`src/kat_vectors.zig` transcribes them verbatim, hex case preserved as
published: 8 secret-key rows that must sign to the exact published signature,
and 11 verify-only rows.

⚠ BIP340 carries a SECOND header the sibling BIPs do not: `License-Code:
BSD-2-Clause OR MIT OR CC0-1.0`, an OR-choice that would let a redistributor of
the BIP's *code* elect CC0 and owe nothing. Whether a CSV of test vectors is the
BIP's "text" (covered by `License:`) or its "code" (covered by `License-Code:`)
is not something this file needs to decide, because it takes the stricter
reading: BSD-2-Clause, reproduced below. Electing the loosest available term to
avoid writing a notice would be choosing the answer first.

As with `modules/psbt` and `modules/bip32`, the BIP publishes no copyright LINE
of its own and `bitcoin/bips` carries no `LICENSE` file (verified 2026-09-09:
HTTP 404). The rightsholder is the BIP's named author, and the absence is
recorded rather than filled in with an invented attribution.

